Why Is Demand Increasing
Growing Vehicle Production: Demand for new vehicles across established and emerging automotive markets supports the need for reliable starting, lighting, and ignition battery systems.
Replacement Battery Requirements: The large installed base of vehicles creates recurring demand for replacement batteries, supporting sales through automotive service centers, distributors, and retail channels.
Increasing Electrical Loads: Modern vehicles require dependable low-voltage power for electronic systems, while start-stop technology is encouraging adoption of enhanced flooded batteries and absorbed glass mat designs.

Automotive SLI Battery Market Watch: EFB and AGM Technology
Automotive SLI batteries remain important for conventional vehicles and also serve as auxiliary power sources in hybrid and electric vehicles. Manufacturers are developing enhanced flooded battery (EFB) and absorbed glass mat (AGM) products to meet the demands of start-stop systems and higher electrical loads. Performance characteristics such as cold-cranking capability, reliability, durability, and compatibility with vehicle electrical systems remain central to product development.

Segmentation Highlights
By Battery Type: Flooded lead-acid and valve-regulated lead-acid batteries serve different price, maintenance, and performance requirements. EFB and AGM designs are relevant for vehicles with more demanding electrical systems.
By Vehicle: Passenger cars and commercial vehicles represent important demand categories, with battery specifications varying by vehicle design and operating conditions.
By Voltage: 12V and 24V battery systems support different vehicle electrical architectures and starting requirements.

